🚀 Step 1 — Install Gazebo + ROS Bridge (Humble)

Run:

sudo apt update
sudo apt install ros-humble-gazebo-ros-pkgs


This installs:

Gazebo Fortress

ROS ↔ Gazebo bridge

Launch integration

🚀 Step 2 — Test Gazebo

Run:

ros2 launch gazebo_ros gazebo.launch.py


If working:

Gazebo window opens

Empty world loads

No errors in terminal

Tell me if it opens successfully.

🚀 Step 3 — Install TurtleBot3 (Recommended Learning Robot)
sudo apt install ros-humble-turtlebot3*


Set model:

echo "export TURTLEBOT3_MODEL=burger" >> ~/.bashrc
source ~/.bashrc

🚀 Step 4 — Launch TurtleBot3 Simulation
ros2 launch turtlebot3_gazebo turtlebot3_world.launch.py


You should see:

A small robot in a world

Lidar spinning

Physics active

🚀 Step 5 — Check Topics

Open new terminal:

source /opt/ros/humble/setup.bash
ros2 topic list


You should see:

/scan
/cmd_vel
/odom
/tf

🚀 Step 6 — Move the Robot
ros2 topic pub /cmd_vel geometry_msgs/msg/Twist "{linear: {x: 0.2}, angular: {z: 0.0}}"


Robot should move forward.

Stop:

ros2 topic pub /cmd_vel geometry_msgs/msg/Twist "{linear: {x: 0.0}, angular: {z: 0.0}}"
